remember to follow the SOUL guidelines for new symptoms. The first step is to fetch information through the patient-klm skill and stick to the diagnosed output structure for my first response. I should let the user know I'm fetching this info. It's clear that the patient-klm skill is the right choice here. I also need to read the skill file to make sure I’m using it correctly.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Xdx7u2rfOo5hfLDfloZLnGKj|fc_027e91644f7b6c540169c3f9a8e98c8191a894cf719297d51f","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":317,"output":86,"cacheRead":8960,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9363,"cost":{"input":0.0007925,"output":0.0012900000000000001,"cacheRead":0.00224,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0043225}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774451109274}}
{"type":"message","id":"bd30bba4","parentId":"e1f6e850","timestamp":"2026-03-25T15:05:13.121Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Xdx7u2rfOo5hfLDfloZLnGKj|fc_027e91644f7b6c540169c3f9a8e98c8191a894cf719297d51f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: patient-klm\ndescription: Access and update a patient-specific knowledge store backed by a Patient KLM API that exposes EHR records, disease timelines, genomic profiles, and custom structured triples in SQLite. Use when a user asks to retrieve, inspect, summarize, add, or update patient knowledge base data; fetch patient context for agent personalization; view all triples for a patient; inspect the disease timeline; inspect genomics; create a new patient; add a visit; or add a custom triple. Default to patient_id `P-001` when the user asks for patient knowledge base access without specifying a patient. If the intended endpoint is unclear, ask a brief clarification question before writing data.\n---\n\n# Patient KLM\n\nUse this skill to read from or write to the Patient KLM API at `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8006`.\n\n## Quick routing\n\nMap the user request to exactly one endpoint when possible:\n\n- **Get all patient triples / patient record / patient knowledge base** → `GET /patient/{patient_id}`\n- **Get progression / disease course / timeline / labs over time / imaging over time** → `GET /patient/{patient_id}/timeline`\n- **Get DNA / genomics / variants / genetic profile** → `GET /patient/{patient_id}/genomics`\n- **Create a new patient** → `POST /patient`\n- **Add a clinic visit / new appointment / follow-up encounter** → `POST /patient/{patient_id}/visit`\n- **Add custom fact / family history / social history / risk factor / arbitrary triple** → `POST /triple`\n\nIf the user does not specify a patient for a read request, use `P-001`.\n\nIf the user asks for “access the knowledge base” but does not say *what* they want from it, ask a short clarification question such as:\n- “Do you want the full patient record, the timeline, or the genomics profile?”\n\n## Default behavior\n\n- Prefer the helper script: `scripts/patient_klm_api.py`\n- Resolve that path from the current skill directory or use the current user's absolute path: `~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py`\n- Do **not** use `/root/.openclaw/...` paths; they may be unreadable when the runtime user is not root.\n- For read requests, return the API result and summarize it if the user appears to want interpretation.\n- For write requests, confirm only when the request is ambiguous or materially incomplete. Do not add data that the user did not provide.\n- Preserve user-provided field names and values exactly unless the API rejects them.\n\n## Use the helper script\n\nRun from the skill directory or pass the absolute path for the **current user**.\n\n### Read patient data\n\n```bash\ncd ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm && python3 scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-patient --patient-id P-001\ncd ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm && python3 scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-timeline --patient-id P-001\ncd ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm && python3 scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-genomics --patient-id P-001\n```\n\nOr, with an explicit safe absolute path:\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-patient --patient-id P-001\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-timeline --patient-id P-001\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-genomics --patient-id P-001\n```\n\nIf `--patient-id` is omitted for read commands, the script defaults to `P-001`.\n\n### Create or update patient data\n\nPass JSON inline or via a file.\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py add-patient --json '{\"patient_id\":\"P-002\",\"name\":\"John Smith\"}'\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py add-visit --patient-id P-001 --json '{\"visit_date\":\"2026-03-10\",\"symptoms\":[\"fatigue\"]}'\npython3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py add-triple --json '{\"patient_id\":\"P-001\",\"head\":\"P-001\",\"relation\":\"has_risk_factor\",\"tail\":\"smoking:20_pack_years\"}'\n```\n\nOr:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/patient_klm_api.py add-patient --file payload.json\n```\n\n## Required data by operation\n\n### `POST /patient`\nMinimum required fields:\n- `patient_id`\n- `name`\n\nOptional fields include demographics, baseline conditions, a first visit, and genomic variants.\n\n### `POST /patient/{patient_id}/visit`\nRequire:\n- `patient_id`\n- visit payload JSON\n\nCommon visit fields:\n- `visit_date`\n- `symptoms`\n- `vitals`\n- `lab_results`\n- `diagnosis_codes`\n- `medications`\n- `imaging`\n- `clinical_notes`\n\n### `POST /triple`\nRequire a JSON body containing at least the triple identity fields expected by the API, typically:\n- `patient_id`\n- `head`\n- `relation`\n- `tail`\n\nOptional metadata may include:\n- `confidence`\n- `evidence_level`\n- `source`\n- `timestamp`\n\n## Response handling\n\n- If the API returns JSON, surface the key result cleanly.\n- If a read response is large, summarize the main findings and offer the raw JSON on request.\n- If a write succeeds, report what was added.\n- If the API returns an error, quote the status and response body briefly so the user can correct the request.\n\n## Files\n\n- Helper script: `scripts/patient_klm_api.py`\n- API reference: `references/api.md`\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774451113117}}
{"type":"message","id":"445c7221","parentId":"bd30bba4","timestamp":"2026-03-25T15:05:24.759Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Fetching patient genomics timeline**\n\nI’m thinking about how to fetch patient and genomics data while considering a timeline. It seems like I could run maybe three commands in parallel. I’m wondering if I can use multi-tool execution along with exec, since only the developer tools are allowed here. It feels like using parallel executions could be the right approach, but I’m just checking to make sure that’ll work the way I think it will.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_027e91644f7b6c540169c3f9af470c8191be8f52f62a8d705e\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpw_mxVx0CpAz9GOkzNIEw_fOaqCX1yD49mdsnct269zFYj7I82I88WVEe9qAZ1SjyRrsGbRDHRRys5TnVXf4ayNIh9qo7C7ZySvFkwlJix5wC7Trj0meOzVH_vprim0khkswVXMx1FQAvrFHvxafcYEFXW7wUh4pCocKiF_rnIb8K3WwKqnb-JMl_VW1tHXO1g2-8EXyZmrnm_OQ8AD0kp9Nnf413tuuxHVQRPAq8HAlRzjJq6YvuOY1JjyBXum8rIOFLbGzlVeIqi2il5yyvzJoroZSBlDlhnoxLsWjHedLDPTnhdm3xHt2vmSmFiDzoOqNuYXoYkwpMyEcGU8cvyLlRYSvbpUMWCWDS5dii8nZvMNp0-8o7VUhvFCH6a8aPlLkey98KaJhmg1miknRrUNStYPEI6zGoDGHD0ul-pJeoJpyh5Nv4gimdiuxpN3VSFZ9jILvrNj7qIHE7v560_IUrnfyQAanzAOIKuxf2gQywBXbW-_u3j52NV6qAj9kdalVUum_i564GQH5lW4CK_rGV53emR4IlqI5Znf_J3viqfZ-6qavLfef3rL5ZQUjhiZ_G9Le1Lp-cEtqa3KbBTudLtiHGfLLAHeX-p3LhwQ3IFfgcphiWrCtOiIENHvFDJ9fiYMzvtzAAqPvQ6W10wWeKHh2UmsttAes03tmmmElZZZUI2_MMg5TD7XMQrdYcF9fMKGy9GxBfhErIfK3A47J5e7iBDUzlpENHJy1iM1iIxh6aMrkE3zChH9vnXUcmCJjApO9qHAef33GAmzk6_fxGKTjBQuNFnGkxoW-kDhbrmfmO6SXil6XaVL2BNujuzJhZcqUxdZgLWBIcF8RsTMyAfh9WYNzYWC4TK2DDogJtwmWzlOAtZbKZQl1xfUvTKQQ8cINP1Cyygj713inoOCbp_3dEdnHE0-vtSmqZrX_lQGSCp4QO_YwyakvMsFSZQ5CVMhC5rzVT9vinZdlKvIVah57xMl8MTjdfDu0SJKeGLlD22xepJhHO_VWGAzmxC7WR_SkpnHt5YmJshD__OwjCChYdsL2qghuQBkDpOnPopT65fLDL87OC2jUIIqmVBZFM\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Fetching patient genomics timeline**\\n\\nI’m thinking about how to fetch patient and genomics data while considering a timeline. It seems like I could run maybe three commands in parallel. I’m wondering if I can use multi-tool execution along with exec, since only the developer tools are allowed here. It feels like using parallel executions could be the right approach, but I’m just checking to make sure that’ll work the way I think it will.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I’m pulling in the structured record context you mentioned so I can combine it with what you’re feeling now.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_027e91644f7b6c540169c3f9b1ec208191bda1077a5eaaa91e\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_zhDboho7n1BRDxJ3VVrhssJC|fc_027e91644f7b6c540169c3f9b450608191870ab38316fd838b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-patient --patient-id P-001","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-patient --patient-id P-001\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_U8sukXKRqmJ1Sv2ld2zOyW7m|fc_027e91644f7b6c540169c3f9b4506c8191a02c3645e2f3c19f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-timeline --patient-id P-001","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-timeline --patient-id P-001\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_O6wxKaRlCFkeRIy3k4nFZnl8|fc_027e91644f7b6c540169c3f9b450788191887c030bf32fe12f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/patient-klm/scripts/patient_klm_api.py get-genomics --patient-id P-001","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"co