aging tool. I might be able to include that MEDIA:url, possibly as a first-class mention? Then, for the final text, I could include the MEDIA:url as well. Additionally, after using the tool, I should consider suggesting LLM distillation, just like mentioned in the SOUL context. Let's make sure everything flows well!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Kidney Cancer Detector**\nThe pipeline labeled this CT image as **kidney tumor**.\nConfidence: **99.99%**\nInference time: **3.27 seconds**\n\n**Image Analyzer**\nThe Image Analyzer also predicted **kidney_tumor**.\nCAM coverage: **0.0128**\nCAM center ratio: **0.825**\nCAM left-right asymmetry: **0.10**\nCAM top-bottom asymmetry: **1.00**\nThe model’s explanation says it focused on a **localized, centrally placed region within the renal tissue**, with an asymmetric pattern that may fit a **localized structural abnormality**. A heatmap image is attached below.\n\n**xAI**\nThe xAI summary says the image shows a **high-likelihood kidney tumor pattern**, with visual evidence considered compatible with kidney cancer on this scan.\nIts confidence interpretation is that the signal is **very strong**, but still **not definitive on its own**.\nRecommended next steps:\n1. Further medical evaluation with imaging and laboratory review\n2. Consultation with your oncology/urology team to interpret the result in context\n3. Consideration of additional diagnostic confirmation if your treating team thinks it is needed\n\n**Result Interpretation**\nThis pipeline result is **concerning** and it fits the symptoms you described earlier: severe right-sided pain, pink urine, major recent weight loss, fatigue, and your prior kidney cancer history. Because you already have a CT from last week and this new image analysis also points toward a tumor pattern, I would strongly recommend that you **contact your oncology/urology team as soon as possible** and have the recent CT formally reviewed if that has not already happened.\n\n**Recommended next steps**\nPlease seek **urgent in-person evaluation today** if the pain is severe now, the urine becomes clearly red, you feel faint, cannot keep fluids down, or urine output drops.\nIf you want, send me the **written CT report from last week**, and I can help interpret it carefully alongside this result.\nThis tool output is a **preliminary signal, not an actual diagnosis**.\n\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/b0f1c107-0576-49f4-985a-1754b3411728.jpeg\n\nIf you want, after we review the CT report, I can also help you use the **LLM Distillation** tool to turn this whole conversation plus the pipeline result into one clear medical summary with suggested next steps.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_027e91644f7b6c540169c3fa97b3c0819184769bd7fcaf0d6a\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":10610,"output":594,"cacheRead":35200,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46404,"cost":{"input":0.026525000000000003,"output":0.00891,"cacheRead":0.008799999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.044235}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774451347667}}
